{
  "requirement": "Habeas MUST apply the SDK's built-in credential rules to source text supplied\nin mandatory inputs, tool reads, and search results, and to source text shown\nin the book and `habeas info`. The same rules apply to configuration files.\n\nEach match of a built-in `secretshape` rule MUST be replaced with\n`[REDACTED:<rule name>]`, preserving every line break. The match MUST extend\nthrough adjacent regions flagged by the entropy heuristic when only whitespace\nseparates them. Entropy alone MUST NOT trigger a replacement.\n\nOutlines MUST use the original source for structure and spans. Structural\nhashes MUST use the redacted text for each matched region as specified in\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.sources.redaction`. The `secretshape` version MUST be\npinned exactly because changes to its rules can affect evidence hashes.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "Add a test, marked {test}`requirements.authoring.redaction`, for the execution-coverage book pages. Put a credential such as `crate::redaction::tests::github_token()` in a Rust doc comment, in `habeas:coverage` citation commentary, in a recorded rationale and FIXME entry, and in a validation error or source-notes diagnostic. Then generate the notes with `src/execution_coverage/notes.rs#fn[entry]` and `src/execution_coverage/book.rs#fn[populate_in]/fn[renumber]`, or the public populate path. Assert the page contains `[REDACTED:GitHub Token]` and not the raw token. — The requirement says redaction MUST apply to source text shown in the book. The execution-coverage notes pages put source-derived text into the book, namely doc comments and citation commentary. They also show recorded rationales, FIXME entries and errors. The code redacts each of these through `redact_text`. None of the reviewed tests, and no test I found under `src/execution_coverage`, generates these pages with a credential and asserts the output is redacted. If `entry` dropped the `redact_text` call on doc comments or commentary, every reviewed test would still pass. `src/index.rs#mod[tests]/fn[detail_pages_and_info_display_redacted_source]` covers only the requirement index detail pages and `habeas info`.",
